{
  "title": "📊 Mean of Grouped Data — Three Powerful Methods",
  "hook": "You have marks of 100 students grouped into class intervals: 0-20, 20-40, 40-60, 60-80, 80-100. How do you find the average? You can't use each individual mark — but the 'class mark' (midpoint) saves the day!",
  "explanation": "<div style=\"background:#F3E5F5;border-left:4px solid #7B1FA2;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0\"><strong style=\"color:#7B1FA2\">Class Mark (xᵢ):</strong> The midpoint of each class interval. xᵢ = (lower limit + upper limit) / 2.</div><p><b>Three methods to find the mean:</b></p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Method</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Formula</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Best when</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\"><b>Direct</b></td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">x̄ = Σfᵢxᵢ / Σfᵢ</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Small values of xᵢ</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\"><b>Assumed Mean</b></td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">x̄ = a + Σfᵢdᵢ / Σfᵢ (dᵢ = xᵢ − a)</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Large values, saves computation</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\"><b>Step Deviation</b></td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">x̄ = a + (Σfᵢuᵢ / Σfᵢ) × h</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Equal class widths (most efficient)</td></tr></table><div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#E3F2FD,#BBDEFB);border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:1.05rem;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-size:0.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:#1565C0;margin-bottom:4px\">Key formula</div><strong>Step Deviation: uᵢ = (xᵢ − a) / h, where a = assumed mean, h = class width</strong></div><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Make a table with columns: Class, fᵢ, xᵢ, fᵢxᵢ (or dᵢ, uᵢ)</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Choose 'a' as the class mark of the middle class</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">For assumed mean / step deviation</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Compute the relevant sums</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div><div><strong>Apply the formula</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div></div><div style=\"background:#FFF8E1;border-left:4px solid #FFB300;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> All three methods give the SAME answer — use the one that's easiest for the given data.</div>",
  "worked_example": "<b>Example:</b> Find the mean for this data:<br><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Class</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">0-10</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">10-20</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">20-30</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">30-40</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">40-50</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">fᵢ</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">5</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">8</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">15</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">12</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">10</td></tr></table><br>Using <b>Step Deviation</b> with a = 25, h = 10:<br><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Class</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">fᵢ</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">xᵢ</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">uᵢ = (xᵢ−25)/10</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">fᵢuᵢ</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">0-10</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">5</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">5</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">−2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">−10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">10-20</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">8</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">15</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">−1</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">−8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">20-30</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">15</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">25</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">0</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">0</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">30-40</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">12</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">35</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">12</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">40-50</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">10</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">45</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">20</td></tr></table><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Σfᵢ = 50, Σfᵢuᵢ = −10+−8+0+12+20 = 14</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>x̄ = 25 + (14/50) × 10 = 25 + 2.8 = 27.8</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div></div>",
  "try_this": {
    "question": "Find the mean (direct method): Classes 10-20 (f=4), 20-30 (f=6), 30-40 (f=10), 40-50 (f=5).",
    "hint": "xᵢ = 15, 25, 35, 45. Σfᵢxᵢ = 4(15)+6(25)+10(35)+5(45).",
    "answer": "Σfᵢxᵢ = 60+150+350+225 = 785. Σfᵢ = 25. Mean = 785/25 = 31.4."
  },
  "fun_fact": "The word 'statistics' comes from the German word 'Statistik' meaning 'science of the state' — it was originally used for collecting census data!"
}